# A100 (SXM4 80GB or 40GB, compute capability 8.0) deployment parameters (one GPU; `--n_gpu 2|4|8` row-shards `big` over P cards). The mode is NOT here: it comes
# from `--mode` or OPENFOLD3_OB0_OPT; no lever switch is written in this file — the mode table is opt/openfold3_ob0_opt/modes.py. usage:
# `run.sh pred|check|warm --config a100 --mode <mode> ...`, or `source configs/a100.env` before calling the package or a kit self-test directly. Every value
# can be pre-set in the environment; this file fills what is unset. It refuses (rc 3, NOT ACTIVE) when openfold3_ob0_opt is not installed on the `python` on
# PATH (every route, the stock route included, goes through the package). Pinned stack: stock/PINS.json "pinned_stack" (python 3.11.5, torch 2.10.0+cu128,
# triton 3.6.0); the Triton cells the fast mode serves on this card are the 8.0-keyed rows of the core's tables (opt_core attn/pair_fused_cells.json,
# kernels/flash_triattn.py) and of the core's fpf_trimul_v4 table (opt_core/kernels/fpf_trimul_v4/table.json) (`8.0|3.6`).
# Per-card differences from configs/h100.env — the complete list; anything not named here is the identical code path and lever set on both cards:
#   1. image: the same pinned stack; where the image carries deepspeed's DS4Sci evoformer_attn op (upstream's `use_deepspeed_evo_attention` switch — off in
#      this kit's stock configuration and in every mode's runner yaml, so no route of this kit loads it), an A100 image is the sm_80-inclusive variant: the op
#      compiled with sm_80 in its TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST; an sm_90-only op fails a caller's DS4Sci runner yaml on this card by name
#      (CUDA: no kernel image is available for execution on the device), never degraded.
#   2. fast, pair cells (levers trimul_v4, triatt_block, pair_transition): the same kernels with this card's launch tiles — the cc 8.0 rows of opt_core
#      attn/pair_fused_cells.json and the `8.0|3.6` cells of the core's fpf_trimul_v4 table (opt_core/kernels/fpf_trimul_v4/table.json) (tiles within sm_80's shared memory);
#      shapes a table does not list keep their per-call routes and census words (`fallback:<reason>=<n>`, exit 0) as on H100.
#   3. fast, template pair stack (c=64): its triangle-attention block is served by the core's cells on both cards (8.0 and 9.0 rows exist for the 64x4x16
#      shape; the `triatt_block` census counts those calls as served) with this card's own launch tiles. The template stack's TriMul stays on the line's
#      own path on both cards (the fused TriMul serves pair widths 128 and 256 only — a documented shape gate, census `fallback:c:64x64`). The template
#      embedder's own kernels (templ_embed) are plain Triton and run on both cards. The transition names the core's `v2_fold` kernel first
#      (TRANSITION_VARIANTS): its rows are compute capability 9.0 rows ((128,512), (64,128), (64,256)), so on this card the pairformer's c=128 transition
#      is served by the v1 row (an 8.0 row exists) and a c=64 transition the tagged blocks reach steps aside by name per call (`fallback:no-cell:...`,
#      counted) — by name, never silent, never a refusal of the run.
#   4. fast, triatt_provider: the core provider's cc 8.0 cells (the sealed triangle-attention package's sm_80 member at both head dims; k2b / k2
#      where it has no prebuilt for the running torch ABI) — the tier word, no per-card setting in this file.
#   5. fast, atom_window: this card's `ln_qkvg` launch tile — row 8.0 of opt/openfold3_ob0_opt/cells/atom_window.py LN_TILE_BY_CC = 32 rows x 8 warps (the core's
#      128-row TF32 tile needs more shared memory per block than sm_80 has: without the row every call raised Triton's OutOfResources and ran the stock block,
#      counted — `served=0 errors=…OutOfResources…`); with the row the lever serves its calls here as on H100 (LEVER line `… errors=none ln_tile=32x8(cc8.0)`).
#      9.0 keeps the core's tile (`ln_tile=core`).
#   6. fast, dit_attn: books `calls=0` under this line on both cards — dit_glue serves the token DiT blocks class-wide (overriding 0.5.0's high-precision ask, named),
#      so dit_attn's seam is reached only for blocks dit_glue refuses; nothing card-specific.
#   7. exact + fast, trunk_graph: captures up to its nmax (1024 tokens) on both cards; above it the pairformer runs eager, named (`fallback=n_tok_gt_nmax`).
#      fast, trimul_v4: `impl=fpf_trimul_v4.generic` here (the kdesc cells are 9.0 rows). trimul_provider (the row per call class from the core's ONE
#      triangle-multiplication provider): the kit row v4 at (128,128) as on H100; the template pair stack's (64,64) keeps `fallback:c:64x64` (the line's TriMul)
#      on this card, where H100 serves a provider row — the ACTIVE line's card_support= word names trimul_provider for it.
#   8. big --n_gpu P: the same chunk plan (the 80 GB-card table, tp.CHUNK_PLAN; a card reporting less memory gets the launcher's NOTE line naming it).
#   9. exact + fast, exactln: the identical code path — the core's LayerNorm replica is compiled by NVRTC for the running compute capability (8.0 here) and
#      proven torch.equal against the statement at install as on 9.0; `exact --det 1` equals `off --det 1` byte for byte here too, with and without the lever.
#      On this card the trunk's bf16 pair / MSA norms gain through the replica and the eager fp32 sampler's pair norms lose; no per-card setting separates the
#      two (both are >= N^2-row classes, so the row floor cannot), and the lever is never switched off by card: it runs here as on H100 and the ACTIVE line's
#      card_support= word names it.
#  10. exact + fast + big, the LayerNorm binding (exactln on the exact line, ln_provider on fast / big): no per-card row floor — the core's LayerNorm
#      provider decides per call class from its cc 8.0 cells (the N^2-row pair / S·N-row MSA norms serve the replica on `exact` and the Triton rows on `fast` /
#      `big`; the N-row / 5N-row / 8N-row operands keep ATen in eager and take the replica or a Triton row under graph replay). The EAGER sampler's C 128
#      pair-norm classes below the pair family's smallest cell keep ATen by name; the classes at or above it are served.
#  11. big, the offload port's item gate: OF3O_GATE_BY_CARD["A100"] equals the H100 value (below) — under it the line IS the fast line as composed, its CUDA
#      graphs included; at or above it the port engages.
# Tested on this card (registry A100_TESTED): exact (cueq), fast, big on one GPU and `big --n_gpu 2` — every lever of those lines; `exact --det 1` equals
# `off --det 1` byte for byte as on H100. The 40GB part runs the same lines and levers; the inputs that fit are smaller, and nothing here is sized from the
# card's memory except one launcher line: `big --n_gpu P` keeps the 80 GB-card chunk plan (tp.CHUNK_PLAN) on a card reporting less than tp.MIN_CARD_BYTES
# and says so (`NOTE chunk plan table (CHUNK_PLAN) is for >=79 GB cards; using it on <m> GB …`, which names the variable that tunes the chunk) — a note,
# never a refusal. A lever of a mode that cannot run on a card is a named refusal of the mode (exit 3), never a silent downgrade; an untested card or library
# version engages the lever with its default settings, named; documented size/shape gates keep their census words and exit 0.
export MODEL_OPT=${MODEL_OPT:-$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)}                                     # this openfold3_ob0/ directory (the package locates the add-ons through it)
export MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU=${MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU:-A100}                                                            # the GPU this configuration targets (compute capability 8.0); check/pred report a mismatch
# The memory line's item gate on this card: modes.OF3O_GATE_BY_CARD["A100"] = 1401 (big below OF3O_MIN_TOKENS polymer tokens — the query's largest member — IS the
# fast line as composed, its CUDA graphs included: fast's sampler cells stay captured there (host-bound when eager); at or above it, and with no token count,
# the offload port engages); the value = the largest input size whose fast-line peak leaves >= 15 % of the card free, + 1 —
# OF3O_MIN_TOKENS=<n>|none pre-set in the environment overrides the table.
# OPENFOLD3_OB0_CKPT is not filled here: the pinned weights are of3-ob-2025-06-30-174k.pt (OpenBind-0), sha256 bd43301c… (stock/PINS.json "weights"),
# and every route hashes the file it is given against that digest (one WEIGHTS line: pinned, or an unknown-checkpoint WARNING — every mode proceeds, labelled weights_pinned=false).
# Set OPENFOLD3_OB0_CKPT (or pass --ckpt) to the pinned bytes (`run.sh install --weights DIR` fetches them); pred / warm refuse by name without one.
[ -n "${OPENFOLD3_OB0_CKPT:-}" ] && export OPENFOLD_CACHE=${OPENFOLD_CACHE:-$(dirname "$OPENFOLD3_OB0_CKPT")}             # upstream's cache directory (entry_points/parameters.py). Upstream reads two things there: a user runner.yml (deep-merged UNDER any --runner-yaml when present —
# the kit names such a merge on stderr when that file exists) and the ckpt_root pointer (unused here: every route passes --inference-ckpt-path). Default: the checkpoint's own
# directory unless the caller sets one; the routes apply the same default without this file (cli.openfold_cache_default). With --inference-ckpt-name (upstream's registry NAME instead of a
# path) upstream resolves the file in its parameter directory under $OPENFOLD_CACHE and refuses by name when it is absent (entry_points/validator.py) — no download at predict time
_of3_err=$(python -c "import openfold3_ob0_opt" 2>&1 >/dev/null) || { _of3_rc=$?; case "$_of3_err" in *"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'openfold3_ob0_opt'"*) echo "[openfold3_ob0-opt] NOT ACTIVE: reason=package_missing: openfold3_ob0_opt is not importable on $(command -v python || echo 'python (not on PATH)') (${_of3_err##*$'\n'}): pip install -e $MODEL_OPT/../common/opt_core -e $MODEL_OPT/opt" >&2; return 3 2>/dev/null || exit 3 ;; esac; printf '%s\n' "$_of3_err" >&2; return "$_of3_rc" 2>/dev/null || exit "$_of3_rc"; }   # the package itself (imports nothing of the core). `package_missing` names ONLY a ModuleNotFoundError of openfold3_ob0_opt; every other failure — the installed .pth hook's by-name refusal at interpreter start under an exported OPENFOLD3_OB0_OPT* (undeclared variable / the core pin gate / producer probe: rc 3) or any import error — is forwarded verbatim with the interpreter's own exit code, never re-diagnosed
python -c "import openfold3_ob0_opt._core_gate as g, os; g.gate(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(g.__file__)), tag='openfold3_ob0-opt')" || { return 3 2>/dev/null || exit 3; }   # the core pin gate (openfold3_ob0_opt/_core_gate.py = the house template): an absent or mismatched opt_core is its NOT ACTIVE line, rc 3, before anything else runs
unset _of3_err _of3_rc
if [ -z "${MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY:-}" ]; then MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY=$(python -c "from openfold3_ob0_opt.modes import jit_cache_key; print(jit_cache_key())") || { echo "[openfold3_ob0-opt] NOT ACTIVE: reason=core_missing: the JIT cache key probe (openfold3_ob0_opt.modes.jit_cache_key) failed on $(command -v python || echo 'python (not on PATH)')" >&2; return 3 2>/dev/null || exit 3; }; fi; export MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY   # the JIT cache key torch<version sans local tag>-cu<CUDA version sans dot>-sm<compute capability digits>, e.g. torch2.10.0-cu128-sm90
# MODEL_OPT_JIT_ROOT (optional): a persistent root for the compiled-kernel caches. When set, the Triton cache is keyed by the running stack under it —
# TRITON_CACHE_DIR=<root>/<MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY>/triton: upstream's own Triton triangle kernels (stock, when its configuration runs them) and the trunk-kernels
# flash triangle attention of `fast` both compile into it — unless pre-set; when unset nothing is exported and Triton uses its default (~/.triton/cache).
if [ -n "${MODEL_OPT_JIT_ROOT:-}" ]; then
  export TRITON_CACHE_DIR=${TRITON_CACHE_DIR:-$MODEL_OPT_JIT_ROOT/$MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY/triton}
  export TORCH_EXTENSIONS_DIR=${TORCH_EXTENSIONS_DIR:-$MODEL_OPT_JIT_ROOT/$MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY/torch_extensions}   # torch C++/CUDA extensions built at first use (the sm80 triangle-attention arm on compute capability 8.0) keyed the same way
fi
export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1                                                                                     # no .pyc in the mounted tree
